[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "I. Summary — Offering of Shares",
    "text": "z. SUMMARY The Wells Fargo Trust for Securities Lending (the “Tru is offering shares. beneficial interest In the Wells Fargo Enhanced Yield Fund tp qualified ‘institutioner purchasers,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "I. Summary — Establishment of Trust",
    "text": "The Trust has been established pursuant to a Declaration of Trust dated October 24, 2000 and as further amended from time to time (the “Declaration of Trust”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "I. Summary — Purpose of Trust",
    "text": "‘The purpose of the Trust is to provide lenders engaged in securities loan \" transactions a continuous source of managed investment for cash collateral,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "I. Summary — Organization of Trust",
    "text": "The Trust Is a Maryland business trust organized under the Annotated Code of Maryland Corporations and Associations, Title 12 Business Trusts."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "I. Summary — Sole Trustee",
    "text": "Wells Fargo Bank Minnesota, N.A. (the “Wells Fargo\") currently serves as the sole trustee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "I. Summary — Shareholder Interests",
    "text": "Subscribers will become beneficial owners (\"Shareholders\") of interests in a Specific Series of the Trust and will be entitied to share. in the Income and gains and losses of that Series upon acceptance of their subscriptions by Wells Fargo and payment of the consideration specified by Wells Fargo from time to time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "IX. The Trustee — Identity",
    "text": "IX. THE TRUSTEE The Trustee Is Wetls Fargo Bank Minnesota, N.A., @ national banking association organized under the. laws of the United States with principal offices in Minneapolis, Minnesota and Columbia, Maryland and is 3 wholly-owned subsidiary of Wells Fargo & Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "IX. The Trustee — Investment Manager Appointment",
    "text": "Wells Fargo has appointed Itself as the investment manager to manage the investments of the Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "IX. The Trustee — Galliard Retention",
    "text": "In that role, Wells Fargo has retained the services of Galliard Capital Management, Inc. (Galllard\") to advise It on managing a portion of the Fund."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "IX. The Trustee — Galliard Affiliation",
    "text": "Galllard [s a wholly owned subsidiary of Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "IX. The Trustee — Allocation Discretion",
    "text": "The Specific portion advised by Galliard will vary from time to time in the sole discretion of Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Shares",
    "text": "Til. TERMS OF THE OFFERING The interest of each Shareholder in the Enhanced Yield Fund (the \"Fund”), a series of the Trust, will be represented by uncertificated shares of beneficial. interest. (the . “Shares\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Proportionate Interest",
    "text": "Each Share represents an undivided proportionate interest in all assets and llabilitles of the Fund and fs without Priority or preference over any other Share."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Initial Price",
    "text": "At the Inception of the Fund, the Initial offering price per share shall be ten dollars ($10.00)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Stable Share Value",
    "text": "Wells Fargo will seek to maintain a relatively stable value per Share, however, no assurance can be given that the Share price will In fact remain stable,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — No Sales Commission",
    "text": "Ne sales commission will be charged by the Fund with respect to any acquisition of Shares."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Purchases and Discontinuance",
    "text": "Wells Fargo Intends to offer Shares for purchase on each Business Day (as defined tn the Declaration of Trust) to Investors at the then applicable value per Share (as - of 12 CONFIDENTIAL defined below), although Wells Fargo reserves the right to discontinue offering the Shares of Enhanced Yield Fund at any time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "III. Terms of the Offering — Minimum Initial Investment",
    "text": "The minimum required investment for the securities lending program, _ Initial purchases will be determined by Wells Fargo In the efficient management of"
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "Valuation of the Trust — Daily Valuation",
    "text": "Valuation of the Trust The assets of the Fund will be valued each Business Day at thelr then current market value."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "Valuation of the Trust — Valuation Services",
    "text": "Wells Fargo will value the assets of the Fund and perform certaln other recordkeeping and accounting services,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "Dividends and Distribution",
    "text": "Dividends and Distribution The ives will declare a dividend on each Business Day, and will pay such dividends monthly."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "Expenses — Fund Expenses",
    "text": "Expenses The Fund will bear all expenses Incurred In connection with ‘the acquisition, ownership and transfer of Its investrnents (including any transfer and withholding taxes, stamp duties, brokerage commissions and other settlement charges, and ‘corporate actions, tax reclamation, transaction and ‘the custodian’s out-of-pocket expenses and charges), the audit expenses of the Trust’s independent auditor associated with the Fund and any indemnification and related expenses as set forth in the Declaration of Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "Expenses — No Wells Fargo Fees",
    "text": "Neither Wells Fargo nor any of its affiliates (including Galliard) will receive any fees or compensation from the Trust for the investment management, custodial, administrative and transfer agent services which it or they provide to the Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Expenses — Forum Accounting Services",
    "text": "Certain of the accounting services for the Trust, however, will be provided by Forum Accounting Services, LLC pursuant to a contract for such services entered into by Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Expenses — Forum Financial Fee",
    "text": "For those services, Forum Financial will receive a fee based on the complexity of the accounting and the average dally net assets of the Fund,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "Expenses — Affiliated Brokers",
    "text": "Subject to any applicable law, Wells Fargo may on occasion use brokers and brokerdealers who are affillates of Wells Fargo to effect transactions on behalf of the Fund."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "Transferability of Shares and Redemption Rights — No Transfer",
    "text": "Transferability of Shares and Redemption Rights Shares of the Fund may not be transferred or assigned."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "Transferability of Shares and Redemption Rights — Redemption Right",
    "text": "However, Shareholders have the right to require the Trust to redeem all or any part of their interest In the Fund at such times as may be permitted by Wells Fargo, but no less often than as of the close of each Business Day, at a redemption price equal to the valuation per _ Share as determined by Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "Transferability of Shares and Redemption Rights — Payment and Suspension",
    "text": "Payment for redeemed Shares will be made in cash within seven days after the redemption date; provided, however, that Wells Fargo reserves the right to postpone payment of the redemption price (without of 12 CONFIDENTIAL liability for interest or income thereon) or to suspend redemption rights In certain circumstances as specified in the Declaration of Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnification — Agent Liability",
    "text": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnifica tion Wells Fargo and other agents of the Trust shall have no lability to the Trust or the Shareholders for any act or omission, provided that such act or omission does not invoive bad falth, willful misconduct, negligence or reckless disregard of Its duties to the Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnification — Agent Indemnity",
    "text": "The Trust has agreed to indemnify Wells Fargo. and other agents of the Trust for any Ifabilities, obligations, losses, damages, taxes, Judgments, and other expenses Incurred by any of them In connection with the Trust If such lability, obligation, loss, damage, tax, judgment or other expense was not caused by such person's own bad faith, willful misconduct, negligence or reckless disregard of its duties under the Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnification — Personal Property",
    "text": "Shares will be deemed to be personal property, giving only the rights provided In the Declaration of Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnification — Shareholder Liability and Title",
    "text": "Under the terms-of the Declaration of Trust, Shareholders will be entitied to the same IImitation of liability extended to stockholders of a business corporation, and ownership of the Shares will not entitle the Shareholders to any title in or to the property of the Trust or the right to call for participation or division of such property for purposes of accounting."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "Limitations of Liability and Indemnification — Shareholder Indemnity",
    "text": "In addition, the Trust will indemnify from the assets of the Trust both past and present Shareholders in the event such Shareholders are held to be personally table for any obligation or liability of the Trust solely by reason of being or having been a Shareholder:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "Amendment of Declaration of Trust",
    "text": "Amendment of Declaration of Trust Because the Declaration does not confer any independent rights to Shareholders not expressly granted under Maryland law, it may be amended by the Trustee at sny time without Shareholder approval, and all Sharehoiders purchase Shares in the ' Fund with notice that the Declaration of Trust may be so amended unless expressly required under.the Maryland Act."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest — Similar Accounts",
    "text": "Conflicts of Interest Wells Fargo provides fiduciary, investment advisory and management services to. various accounts, some of which may invest In the same or similar types of securities as those In which the Fund will invest."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest — Other Investment Funds",
    "text": "In addition, Wells Fargo or its affillates may In the future organize other investment funds to acquire such securities,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest — Nonexclusive Obligations",
    "text": "Thus, the | obligations of Wells Fargo to the Trust are not exclusive."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest — Independent Decisions",
    "text": "The Investment decisions. for the Fund are made Independently from those other accounts managed by Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest — Differing Decisions",
    "text": "Wells Fargo shall be permitted to make an Investment decision on behalf of the Fund which differs from decisions made for, or advice given to, such other accounts even though the investment objectives of such accounts may be the same or similar to the Investment objective of the Trust."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "Auditors",
    "text": "Auditors KPMG LLP seives as Independent auditors for the Trust and Wells Fa continue In that capacity at the sole discretion of Wells Fargo."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "IV. Performance History",
    "text": "IV. PERFORMANCE HISTORY The Enhanced Yield Fund will commence 0 erations on July 2 | has no performance history. p y 2, 2001. Accordingly, It"
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "V. Investment Objectives — Return Objective",
    "text": "V. INVESTMENT OBJECTIVES AND POLICIES investment Objectives , ‘The Fund seeks to achieve a positive return compared to the dally Fed Funds rate b investing In high-quality United States dollar-denominated: securities where the prime considerations for such investments are safety of principal and daily liquidity requirements."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "V. Investment Objectives — Rate Structures",
    "text": "The Fund may Invest in securities wi har ide a y : th fixed, variable, or floating"
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "V. Investment Objectives — Stable Price",
    "text": "The Fund will endeavor to maintain a stable $10.00 price per Share, although no assurance can be given that It will achieve its Investment objective or maintain a Stable Share value."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (a) Portfolio Quality",
    "text": "Investment Policies Investments for the Fund shall comply with the following portfolio guidelines: (a) Portfollo Quality The Trust may only invest in U.S. dollar-denominated obligations rated ‘in the highest short-term rating category by one of two nationally recognized statistical reporting organizations (an “NRSRO*). As such, the Trust can invest in obligations that at the time of purchase (i) have recelved the highest short-term rating by at least one Nationally Recognized Statistical Rating Organization (NRSROs) such as *Ai* by Standard & Poor's and “P-1* by Moody’s Investors Service, Inc.; or (i!) are unrated, but are determined to be of comparable quality by Wells Fargo In fts role as the Investment Manager."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) Portfolio Diversification — Authorized Investments",
    "text": "(b) Portfolio Diversification The Investment Manager is authorized to invest assets of the Fund In: ¢ U.S. Treasury and Government sponsored Agency obligations, e Repurchase agreements, Case 1:09-cv-00041-WDM -BNB ‘Document 294-4 Filed 08/12/10 USDC Colorado Page 9 | of 12 CONFIDENTIAL | * Domestic and foreign bank obligations, and bankers’ acceptances, . Commercial paper and participations, Mortgage-backed securities, Mortgage: pass-through securities, Taxable municipal securitles, Asset-backed securities, and Corporate notes, bonds, debentures @es#e#ss¢"
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) — Issuer Concentration",
    "text": "The Fund cannot Invest more than 5% Of fts assets at the time of purchase in obligations of any one issuer, except for obligations Issued or guaranteed by the U. S. Government, Its. agencies and instrumentalities or repurchase ‘agreements collateralized by such obligations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) — Variable Rate Limit",
    "text": "The Fund may not invest more than 35% of Its total assets at the time of purchase in variable rate securities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) — Illiquid Securities Limit",
    "text": "A maximum of 15% of the Fund's total assets may be Invested in illiquid securities as that term is defined in the SEC's Rule 2a-7,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) — Private Placement Liquidity",
    "text": "Private placement obligations (e.g. Rule 144A Securities) will generally be considered iquid unless at least two broker/dealers provide an active secondary market (trade date plus three business days settlement, market bid quotations).."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (b) — Overnight Maturity",
    "text": "At least 20% of the Fund’s total assets will be Invested in assets scheduled to mature overnight,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (c) Portfolio Maturity — Average Maturity",
    "text": "(c) Portfolio Maturity The maximum dollar-weighted average maturity of the Trust‘s portfolio will be 90 days."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (c) — Maturity Calculation",
    "text": "For purposes of determining the dollar-weighted average maturity of the Trust’s portfollo, the maturity of any obligation is deemed to be the shortest of the following: (i) the stated maturity date of the obligation; (if) the next Interest rate reset for variable rate obligations: or (ii) the next put exercise date {for obligations - with put features), However, for purposes of determining the maturity of a variable rate demand obligation, the maturity is deemed to be equal to the longer of the period of time remaining until the next readjustment of the Interest rate or the period of time remaining unt# the principal amount can be recovered from the issuer on demand."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (d) Maturity of Portfolla Instruments — Maximum Maturity",
    "text": "(d) Maturity of Portfolla Instruments The maximum maturity of a security shall be five years."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (d) — Variable and Floating Rate Maturity",
    "text": "For purposes of determining the maturity of variable and floating rate obligations, the shorter of the period remalning until the next adjustment of the Interest rate or the period remaining until the principal amount can be recovered through demand will be used."
  },
  {
    "id": "c057",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (d) — Repurchase Agreement Maturity",
    "text": "Repurchase agreements shall mature In one year or less."
  },
  {
    "id": "c058",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (d) — Repurchase Agreement End Date",
    "text": "For purposes of determining the maturity of obligations subject to repurchase agreements the end date of the agreement, and not the maturities of the underlying obligation are utilized,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c059",
    "name": "V. Investment Policies (e) Security Downgrades",
    "text": "(e} Security Downgrades In the event that a security held In the Fund ceases to have the highest rating from the Requisite NRSROs or, In the case of an Unrated Security, the Investment Manager determines that it ts no longer of comparable quality, the Investment determines is In the best Interests of the Trust and its shareholders."
  },
  {
    "id": "c060",
    "name": "Other Investment Companies",
    "text": "Other Investment Companies The Fund may invest in the securities of registered and unregistered investment companies to the extent permitted by law (1.e., a registered money market mutual! fund subject to Rule 2a-7 of the Investment Company Act of 1940, as amended, or an unregistered investment company conforming to the requirements of Rule 2a-7). ue"
  },
  {
    "id": "c061",
    "name": "Investment Restrictions — Money Market Index",
    "text": "investment Restrictions All variable rete obligations must be based upon a leading money market index such as Fed Funds or LIBOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c062",
    "name": "Investment Restrictions — Prohibited Floaters",
    "text": "Dual index and inverse floaters are specifically prohibited,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c063",
    "name": "VI. Risk Factors — Investment Value",
    "text": "VI. RISK FACTORS The value of the Shares witl change with the change in value of the Trust's investments. Many factors can affect those values,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c064",
    "name": "VI. Risk Factors — Credit Risk",
    "text": "Because the Trust Invests in debt securities, such as notes and bonds, the Trust Is subject to credit risk and interest rate risk. If the issuer or guarantor of a debt security or the counterparty to a derivative or repurchase agreement is unable or unwilling to make timely principal and/or Interest payments or to otherwise honor its obligations, the value of the related debt security may decline. Debt securities are consequently subject to varying degrees of credit risk, which Is often reflected In the credit rating given to a particular security."
  },
  {
    "id": "c065",
    "name": "VI. Risk Factors — Interest Rate Risk",
    "text": "interest rate risk is the risk that Interest rates may increase, which would reduce the resale value of the securitles held by the Trust (Including any Investments In U.S, Government obligations). Those debt securities with longer durations tend to be more sensitive to changes In Interest rates, usually making them more volatile in value than securities with shorter durations. In 6 of 12 . CONFIDENTIAL addition, changes in market interest rates may also. extend or shorten the duration of certain types of investments, such as asset-backed or mortgagebacked securities, and can affect the value and the related return on the Trust’s investments,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c066",
    "name": "VI. Risk Factors — Liquidity Risk",
    "text": "Liquidity risk may be a'risk factor for the Trust when it invests in particular Investments which are difficult to purchase or sell, The Trust's investment in Nliquid securities may reduce the returns of the Trust because it may be unable to sell the liliquid securities at an advantageous time or price,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c067",
    "name": "VII. Regulatory Considerations — Securities Definition",
    "text": "VII. REGULATORY CONSIDERATIONS Securitles Act of 1933 : The Fund Shares offered hereby are “securities” as defined In the Securities Act of 1933, as amended (the “Securities Act”), and state securities laws."
  },
  {
    "id": "c068",
    "name": "VII. Regulatory Considerations — Registration Requirement",
    "text": "The Securities Act provides, among other things, that no sale of any securities may be made except pursuant to a registration statement which has been filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (“SEC”) and has become effective, unless such sale fs (or the securities sold are) specifically exempted from registration. Most state securities laws have analogous provisions."
  },
  {
    "id": "c069",
    "name": "VII. Regulatory Considerations — Unregistered Offering",
    "text": "The offering and sale of the Fund Shares have not been registered under the Securities Act,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c070",
    "name": "VII. Regulatory Considerations — No Regulatory Review or Approval",
    "text": "This Memorandum has not been reviewed by the SEC, nor has the SEC or ary state securities commission or regulatory authority approved, passed upon or endorsed the merits of this offering."
  },
  {
    "id": "c071",
    "name": "VII. Regulatory Considerations — Private Placement Exemptions",
    "text": "The offering and proposed sale of Shares described herein will be made privately to a limited number of investors (1) in reliance upon the “private placement” exemption from registration provided in Section 4{2) of the Securities Act and Rute 506 of the SEC’s Regulation D and (il) where available; upon elther appropriate exemptions from state registration or qualification requirements, or pursuant to such registration or qualification."
  },
  {
    "id": "c072",
    "name": "Investment Company Act of 1940 — Intended Exemption",
    "text": "Investment Company Act of 1940 It is intended that the Fund be exempt from the registration requirements of the 1946 Act."
  },
  {
    "id": "c073",
    "name": "Investment Company Act of 1940 — Section 3(c)(1) Reliance",
    "text": "The Trust will rely upon, among other things, the exemption contained In Section 3(c)(1) of the 1940 Act, which exempts issuers whose outstanding shares are beneficially owned by not more than 100 persons and who does not propose to make a public offering of Its securities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c074",
    "name": "Investment Company Act of 1940 — Purchaser Representations",
    "text": "Wells Fargo will obtain appropriate representations and undertakings from purchasers of Shares to assure that the conditions of “beneficial ownership” are met on an ongoing basl"
  },
  {
    "id": "c075",
    "name": "ERISA Considerations",
    "text": "ERISA Considerations ERISA Imposes certain dutles and restrictions on those employee benefit plans to - which it applies (*Plans”) and on those persons who are fiduciaries with respect to such Plans, Fiductaries should review with their legal advisors whether the purchase of 12 CONFIDENTIAL or holding of Shares could give rise to a transaction prohibited or not otherwise permissible under the rules and regulations of the United States Department of"
  },
  {
    "id": "c076",
    "name": "Tax Matters — Partnership Classification",
    "text": "Tax Matters The Trust and the Fund are classified as partnerships for Federal income tax purposes."
  },
  {
    "id": "c077",
    "name": "Tax Matters — Transfer Restrictions",
    "text": "Wells Fargo intends to restrict transfers of ownership in order to minimize the risk of the Fund being classified.as a “publicly traded partnership"
  },
  {
    "id": "c078",
    "name": "Tax Matters — Federal Tax Allocation",
    "text": "As a consequence of such status, the Fund will not Itself be subject to Federal income tax . but each Shareholder of the Fund will be allocated a portion of income, gain, loss and deduction, as determined according to the Declaration of Trust,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c079",
    "name": "Tax Matters — KPMG Tax Opinion",
    "text": "The federal income tax consequences to Shareholders of an investment in Shares of the Fund will be passed on by KPMG LLP,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c080",
    "name": "Tax Matters — Maryland Tax",
    "text": "The Fund should be exempt from taxation by the State of Maryland and ownership of Shares In the Fund, absent any other nexus to Maryland, should not cause a Shareholder to be subject to tax in Maryland."
  },
  {
    "id": "c081",
    "name": "Tax Matters — Investor Tax Advice",
    "text": "Investors should, however, consult with their own tax advisers for advice as to the tax consequences to them of an _ Investment In the Trust for both Federal and state income tax purposes."
  },
  {
    "id": "c082",
    "name": "VIII. Additional Information — Purpose",
    "text": "VITX. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION . The purpose of this Memorandum Is to provide an overview. of the Fund and its policies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c083",
    "name": "VIII. Additional Information — Declaration Availability",
    "text": "A complete copy of the.Dectaration of Trust can be obtained during regular business hours from the offices of Wells Fargo at Sixth and Marquette, MAC N9305- 080, Minneapolis, Minnesota."
  },
  {
    "id": "c084",
    "name": "VIII. Additional Information — Review of Materials",
    "text": "Prospective Investors are invited to review the Declaration of Trust and any other materials available to Wells Fargo relating to the Trust and the terms of offering."
  },
  {
    "id": "c085",
    "name": "VIII. Additional Information — Questions and Contact",
    "text": "Representatives of Wells Fargo are available to answer any questions about the Trust and Its Investment related services and can be reached at (612) 667-5464,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c086",
    "name": "Confidentiality — Reproduction and Distribution",
    "text": "Any reproduction or distribution of this confidential offering memorandum, in whole or in part, or the divulgence of any of its contents without the prior written consent of Wells Fargo Is prohibited."
  },
  {
    "id": "c087",
    "name": "Confidentiality — Return of Memorandum",
    "text": "By accepting this offering memorandum, the recipient agrees to return the same to Wells Fargo promptly upon delivery of updated offering materials, upon reaching a decision not to subscribe, or if such subscription is not accepted by Wells Fargo."
  }
]

input.content:
{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The offering is described as made to \"qualified institutional purchasers,\" which cannot be squared with the cover legend furnishing the Memorandum to \"qualified institutional or accredited investors\" or with the Declaration of Trust's Recital (b) and the Subscription Agreement's representation that each subscriber is a \"qualified purchaser.\" Who is eligible to buy Shares therefore turns on which of these three formulations governs.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Declaration is incorporated \"as further amended from time to time,\" so it is unclear whether the terms described in this Memorandum are those in force on October 24, 2000 or whatever the Trustee later substitutes under the amendment power described in the \"Amendment of Declaration of Trust\" provision. The provision fixes no date at which the governing text is ascertained.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This purpose statement — a \"continuous source of managed investment for cash collateral\" — is of the kind argued to control the operative investment terms, and it sits against the Portfolio Diversification list and the five-year maximum maturity provision, which permit long-dated and illiquid holdings. Whether the stated purpose limits those guidelines is open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Currently serves as the sole trustee\" leaves the trusteeship contingent, while Declaration §§2.2–2.3 permit the Trustee to add or appoint successor trustees without Shareholder action. The Memorandum nowhere states what becomes of the described arrangements if the trustee changes.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
 ]},
